From 1ffe25873ea6f49f0c8aee485f31612c1cea49c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:14:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/47] Z 6III MCU link: frames intact both ways, compare
 timers, M4 debuggable

With the body MCU's image on the M4 and SPI1/SPI4 bridged to serial
instances 0/1, the version exchange crossed but everything the MCU sent
after it arrived misaligned: the bridge took the MCU's bytes from its
SPI4 DMA stream before asking whether the EXPEED's instance had a word
queued to clock them, so whenever that instance's 64-word FIFO ran dry
mid-frame the bytes were dropped and the EXPEED read the 128-word frame
from wherever the stream had got to. The bridge now asks the instance
first. With that, the whole start-up conversation runs with every frame
passing both sides' checks: power status, battery (and the multi-frame
battery information), keys, lens, mode, and families 7/15/16/17.

- Z63_MCU_FRAME names each frame both ways by its header (family,
  route, kind, length, count/index, checksum), first four of each kind
  in full and then a count, instead of the first 32 raw words.
- mcu-spi-peer= defaults to 1:0+4:1, the pairing the frame checks of
  both firmwares now confirm.
- TIM2-5 output compare on all four channels, as RM0386 has it: the
  counter reaching CCRx sets CCxIF and, with CCxIE, interrupts. The MCU
  firmware's one-shot delays are CCRx = CNT + n; its shutter service
  powers the shutter's position sensors (PA11), waits 30 ticks on TIM3
  channel 3, then reads them (PC6/PC7, active low; position 2 = both
  low). Without the match the service never finished, the mechanism
  manager left the EXPEED's family-9 mode command unanswered, and the
  EXPEED posted camera error 0x34. Now the MCU reports the shutter ready
  (family 9 kind 1, status 0) and no error is raised. This replaces the
  channel-1-only periodic version, which for CCRx = CNT + n waited
  CNT + n ticks. Matches are settled lazily, so polled PWM channels cost
  nothing per period.
- The A53s are CPU cluster 0 and the M4 cluster 1, so QEMU's gdbstub
  shows them as two inferiors; z63-tools/mcu_probe.py attaches to the
  M4 of a running machine (-gdb tcp:127.0.0.1:41234), breaks, prints
  registers and a rough stack walk. Without the A53 cluster, adding the
  M4's would have left the A53s in an unattached default process.
- mcu-wires= parsing read %u into uint8_t fields; now %hhu.

Where it stands: the GUI draws nothing, as it did with the synthetic
peer and mcu-camctl-reply=on -- it waits on live view. The EXPEED has
not raised the capture-sync request (GPIO port 3 bit 12) yet, and its
family-10 pass-through request (opcode 5, target 0x12) still gets no
reply from the MCU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
